From 3db7103ae752a65e5068b015ba842a1ed3f6ed95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:09:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Gate unissued diagnostic commands on canonical
 prerequisites

Why: frozen administrative phases cannot rotate identity after a transient refusal. A premature escalation or unavailable deployment could stall unrelated sync behind the diagnostic. Classify server clock and exact canonical root as pre-issuance prerequisites; preserve original bytes and deadlines and allow unrelated pending work to proceed.

Bound root eligibility probes to 32 per selection with durable rotation across restart, including quarantined candidates. Memoize capability outages per selection, gate contract capability too, and keep network work outside writer transactions. Do not change issued stream custody; this Core sender uses legacy operations and has no STRICT issuer.

Proof: early diagnostic producer regression RED then GREEN; contract unsupported/capability outage RED then GREEN. Real SQLite->local Board55354df HTTP/DO->replica/restart and unrelated progress composed proof passes for both early clock and missing root. Full sync/retain consumers and scripts/check run separately. Board missing-root/early settlement and immutable conflict proofs live in paired PR205. No producer activation or original incident mutation; no execution/release authority.
